From 85422f4a643d0c0e2e1e6cc61baacd51a1fb69af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:35:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] cpuidle: psci: init after the deferred probes

The CPU PM domains can wait for a parent domain (the vMPM on MSM8996) and a faux device cannot defer its probe, so run psci_idle_init at late_initcall_sync. Without this, cpuidle-psci gives up at device_initcall and the CPUs only use WFI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
index dcf20ea5e..377a12f52 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
@@ -489,4 +489,8 @@ static int __init psci_idle_init(void)
 
 	return 0;
 }
-device_initcall(psci_idle_init);
+/*
+ * After the deferred probes: the CPU PM domains can wait for a parent domain
+ * (the MPM on MSM8996), and a faux device cannot defer its probe.
+ */
+late_initcall_sync(psci_idle_init);
